{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the distinct sound of chimes, not his usual alarm. Sunlight streamed through a window depicting a vibrant, pixelated forest. He sat up, disoriented, and noticed his hands were unnaturally smooth, almost… plastic. He glanced around his room, which wasn't his room at all. It was a cozy cottage with oversized, blocky furniture and a thatched roof. A digital fireplace crackled merrily, spewing out shimmering, green flames. A small, wooden sign on the table read: \"Welcome to Eldoria, Adventurer!\" Arthur's heart hammered against his ribs. He reached out and touched the wooden table; it felt solid, yet somehow… rendered. A wave of nausea washed over him as a cheerful, synthesized voice announced, \"Level 1 initiated. Quest: Find the Lost Amulet of Azmar.\"\n\n***\n\nPanic clawed at Arthur. He tried to speak, but only a digitized \"Huh?\" escaped his lips. He looked down at his body – he was clad in leather armor, complete with a glowing sword at his hip.  The pixelated forest outside his window seemed to pulse with life, the trees rendered with impossibly sharp detail. He was no longer Arthur Penhaligon, accountant; he was a character in a video game. The quest felt absurd, utterly unreal. He cautiously stepped outside, the ground feeling strangely springy beneath his boots. A small, furry creature with large, expressive eyes scurried past, leaving a trail of shimmering dust. Arthur knew, with a chilling certainty, that his life had irrevocably changed. He was trapped, a player in someone else’s world, forced to navigate a digital landscape with a quest he didn’t understand and a destiny he couldn’t control.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.5083379745483398}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.003836772171780467}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.007919815368950367}, {"toke